t index.html is explicitly self-labeled inside the file as a 'Demo snapshot -- live data from automotive.store / clojure -M:dev:run', i.e. a manually pasted REPL output, not build-time-generated either -- the same architectural gap just diagnosed in 5820, left honestly unresolved rather than glossed over.", :event/verification "Ground truth established by direct inspection of a fresh clone (gh repo clone --depth 1, then git fetch --unshallow for full history), not by trusting either iteration 2's prior claim or the promotion ADR's prose: (1) recursive grep for any generate/render script across the whole isic-5820 tree -- zero hits beyond a doc-only mention in operator-quickstart.md; (2) git log --follow -- docs/index.html -- exactly 1 commit, a flat insert, no companion script commit; (3) read the actual HTML content and found concrete, checkable proof of hand-authorship (wrong CTA link target, unfilled 'governor'/'maturity unknown' placeholders, wrong business-type description); (4) curl'd the ADR's cited itonami.cloud/isic-5820/ URL live and confirmed it serves the generic cockpit shell, not 5820-specific content; (5) for the isic-2910 registration, read its .github/workflows/pages.yml (confirms it deploys docs/ as static content, no regeneration step) and the literal 'Demo snapshot' caption inside its own docs/index.html before assigning any score -- did not guess. This is independent verification of live repo state, not a self-report.", :event/not-done "Did not write a new generate.cljs / build-time HTML renderer for isic-5820 -- correctly out of scope for a single bounded iteration per the guardrail, and left as an explicit open gap for a future iteration (or human decision) rather than faked. Did not demote or remove isic-5820 from the flagship cohort table -- only annotated it. isic-2910 was registered as a candidate row only, not promoted to flagship; it independently has the same demo-generation gap as 5820 and would need that closed (among other checklist 